              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ગાર્ડ — gārḍ — \"a guard (on a train or at a gate)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ટ્રેનના છેલ્લા ડબ્બામાં ગાર્ડ બેસે છે. ṭrennā chellā ḍabbāmā̃ gārḍ bese che. The guard sits in the last carriage of the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ગાર્ડ (gārḍ) is borrowed from English guard: on the railway, the guard who rides at the back of the train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
